From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: List a directory by its name on PS5.

NtQueryDirectoryFile enters the directory with fchdir() on the
descriptor the server sent. A PS5 title cannot change its working
directory, so each module emulates one, recording the path every
descriptor it opens was opened by. A descriptor received from the
in-process server has no recorded path in ntdll, fchdir() fails, and no
directory can be listed: no fonts are found and FindFirstFile finds
nothing. On PS5, when fchdir() fails, enter the directory by the name
the server opened it with.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -2893,6 +2893,31 @@
 }
 
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           enter_directory
+ *
+ * Make a directory handle's descriptor the working directory.
+ */
+static int enter_directory( HANDLE handle, int fd )
+{
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    char *unix_name;
+    int ret;
+
+    if (fchdir( fd ) != -1) return 0;
+    /* The descriptor came from the in-process server, so this module's
+     * working-directory emulation knows no path for it: enter the directory
+     * by the name the server opened it with. */
+    if (server_get_unix_name( handle, &unix_name )) return -1;
+    ret = chdir( unix_name );
+    free( unix_name );
+    return ret;
+#else
+    return fchdir( fd );
+#endif
+}
+
+
 /******************************************************************************
  *              NtQueryDirectoryFile   (NTDLL.@)
  */
@@ -2957,7 +2982,7 @@
     mutex_lock( &dir_mutex );
 
     cwd = open( ".", O_RDONLY );
-    if (fchdir( fd ) != -1)
+    if (enter_directory( handle, fd ) != -1)
     {
         if (!(status = get_cached_dir_data( handle, &data, fd, mask, restart_scan )))
         {
